---
description: Windjammer (.wj) coding rules
globs: ["**/*.wj"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Windjammer is a Rust-family language with inferred ownership; it is not in your training data.
Do not write Rust syntax. Use `wj docs <terms>` to look up methods and idioms (offline).

Loop for every edit: `wj check --json <path>` then `wj run --interpret <file>` then
`wj test --interpret .` then `wj build`.

- `println("${x}")`, never `println!`; `[1, 2]`, never `vec![]`; no semicolons; no trailing `return`.
- No `#[derive]`, no `&`/`&mut` arguments, no `.iter()`, no `.unwrap()`/`.expect()`, no `"lit".to_string()`.
- Mutation needs `let mut`; method receivers are plain `self`.
- Handle `Result`/`Option` with `match`, `?`, `unwrap_or`; print them with `${x:?}`.
- Sort `HashMap` keys before printing. Tests live in `*_test.wj` as `@test` functions.
